        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi, @tobiwild!\r\n\r\nI have finally found time and motivation to work on this.\r\n\r\nThe exact changes in your PR couldn't be merged because they break some important features (like allow matching while cursor is on the first and last whitespaces **but** don't include them in textobject). But your approach of refactoring to handle separator spans instead of points gave me a push to implement support of full Lua patterns as separator instead of single characters.\r\n\r\nChanges are in [ai-separator-span](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/tree/ai-separator-span) branch. It has soft deprecation of `separators` (plural) option in favor of `separator` (singluar) one. You use case of matching whitespace should be covered with this setup:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal ai = require('mini.ai')\r\nai.setup({\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    a = ai.gen_spec.argument({ separator = '%s*,%s*' }),\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nCould you, please, test it on your end? I plan to merge it latest by the end of the week. Thanks!",
            "created_at": "2023-02-02T19:15:41Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/187#issuecomment-1414238192",
